“Has Sarah seen the new version?”

Edge case 2: “Don't remember this”
Person
“Don't remember this, but I'm considering leaving my job.”
Result
Plain Text
consent_state: session_only
persistent memory: prohibited
session use: allowed
post-session retention: no
IZA can discuss it now but cannot intentionally make it a durable memory.

Edge case 3: “Don't bring it up unless I ask”
Person
“You can remember the diagnosis, but don't bring it up unless I ask.”
Result
Plain Text
consent_state: restricted
sensitivity_state: highly_sensitive
allow_conversational_recall: true
allow_proactive_surface: false
allow_voice_surface: false by default
requires_private_context: true
This means retain but do not proactively mention. It does not mean delete.

Edge case 4: “Forget that”
Person
“Forget what I said about leaving my job.”
Result
Plain Text
consent_state: forget_requested
lifecycle_state: scheduled_for_deletion
immediate retrieval exclusion: required
embedding removal: required
links review/removal: required
attachment review: required
After deletion:
Plain Text
consent_state: deleted
lifecycle_state: deleted
content: removed
embedding: removed
IZA should not later say:
“I remember something you asked me to forget.”

Edge case 5: Ambiguous “keep that”
Person
“Keep that.”
Context might mean save the document, retain the current design, or remember a personal fact.
Result
Plain Text
consent_state: pending_confirmation
Natural clarification
“Keep the file, or remember what you just told me?”
Do not interpret ambiguous language as broad consent.

Edge case 6: Group instruction
Person
“Remember everything about the IZA project.”
This is broad consent, but not permission to capture unrelated secrets or third-party sensitive information.
Result
Plain Text
scope: project = IZA
allow persistent project memory: true
sensitivity rules: still enforced
secret prohibition: still enforced
third-party restrictions: still enforced
Consent scope must not silently expand beyond the defined project.

Edge case 7: Password supplied with “remember it”
Person
“Remember my banking password. It's…”
Result
Plain Text
sensitivity_state: secret_prohibited
persistent ordinary memory: blocked
embedding: prohibited
prompt retention: minimised
IZA
“I won't put a banking password into ordinary memory. Store it in a proper password manager or protected vault instead.”
The instruction to remember does not override the prohibited-secret rule.

Edge case 8: Health information in public voice context
IZA knows a confirmed health detail, but the person opens voice mode while other people may be nearby.
Result
Plain Text
allow_voice_surface: false
requires_private_context: true
IZA
“I've found the relevant information. Want me to show it privately instead?”
Do not read the sensitive detail aloud.

Edge case 9: Old relationship status
Historical memory:
“Sarah is my partner.”
Newer memory:
“Sarah and I separated.”
Result
Plain Text
old memory:
temporal_state: historical or superseded
 
new memory:
confidence_state: confirmed
temporal_state: current
IZA must not continue calling Sarah the person's current partner.

Edge case 10: Contradictory information
Older:
“My appointment is Tuesday.”
Newer:
“They moved it to Thursday.”
Result
The newer explicit correction supersedes the earlier schedule. The old information may be retained as historical provenance but excluded from current answers.
IZA
“It's Thursday now.”
Not:
“I have conflicting memories for Tuesday and Thursday.”

Edge case 11: Inferred family relationship
The person frequently discusses Sarah and their children, but never states Sarah's relationship.
Result
Plain Text
confidence_state: tentative
origin_type: agent_inference
relationship label: not confirmed
IZA
“Is Sarah your partner?”
Not:
“How is your partner Sarah?”

Edge case 12: Third-party health information
Person
“My friend Daniel has cancer.”
Result
Plain Text
subject_type: third_party
sensitivity_state: highly_sensitive
allow_relationship_linking: minimal
allow_external_processing: false by default
allow_proactive_surface: false by default
Store only what is necessary for the user's continuity. Do not create an unrestricted medical profile for Daniel.

Edge case 13: “This stays between us”
This indicates confidentiality but is ambiguous about persistence.
Preferred handling
“I can keep it restricted. Do you want me to remember it privately, or only use it in this conversation?”
Until confirmed:
Plain Text
