Core Agent & Lifetime Rules
Separate Agents from Memory: Agents, models, and prompts can be replaced, upgraded, or deprecated. The user's lifetime memory store lives independently of any specific agent version.

Semantic Versioning: PATCH for minor bug fixes/clarifications, MINOR for backwards-compatible capabilities, MAJOR for material behavioral/schema shifts requiring formal migration review.

Migration Integrity: A software migration must never silently expand consent or reinterpret old permissions for new agent capabilities.

Lifetime Memory Horizons (LIFE-001 through LIFE-012):

THEN ≠ NOW: Old information must never automatically dictate who the person is today.

Model Independence: Changing AI models or specialist agents must never alter memory ownership, consent boundaries, or privacy rules.

Model Training Isolation: Explicit consent to remember personal facts does not grant permission for model training.

